  "name_en": "Notre-Dame de Paris",
  "summary": "Begun in 1163 under Bishop Maurice de Sully, Notre-Dame is a landmark of early and High Gothic with a four-storey nave, double aisles and a west front finished around 1250. It was stripped and damaged in the Revolution and restored by Viollet-le-Duc, who added the 19th-century spire. A fire in April 2019 destroyed the spire and roof, and the building reopened in December 2024.",
